## 3. Milestones Completed

### Milestone 1 — Project Setup & Authentication
- Django project scaffolding with modular app structure
- Custom `User` model with JWT authentication
- Login, Register, Logout endpoints
- Password reset via email (console backend for dev)
- React frontend with React Router
- AuthContext and `useAuth` hook
- Protected and public route definitions

### Milestone 2 — Database Integration & Models
- [Vessel](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/models.py#4-49) model with all AIS fields (IMO, position, speed, heading, flag, cargo, operator)
- [Port](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/ports/models.py#4-33) model with congestion metrics
- [Voyage](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/frontend/src/pages/VoyageReplayPage.jsx#18-46) model linking vessels to ports with status tracking
- [VesselEvent](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/models.py#78-121) model for journey waypoints
- [SafetyEvent](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/models.py#123-166) model with geographic radius zones
- [VesselSubscription](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/models.py#51-76) model for user alerts
- Database indexes for performance on query-heavy fields
- [seed_baseline.py](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/management/commands/seed_baseline.py) — initial seeding command
- [seed_large_data.py](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/management/commands/seed_large_data.py) — large dataset seeder (150 vessels, 61 ports, 369 voyages)

### Milestone 3 — Backend APIs & Real-time Data
- `GET /vessels/` — Searchable vessel registry (filter by name, type, flag, cargo)
- `GET /vessels/<id>/` — Single vessel detail
- `GET /vessels/<id>/events/` — Per-vessel event history
- `POST /vessels/<id>/subscribe/` — Subscribe to vessel alerts
- `DELETE /vessels/<id>/unsubscribe/` — Unsubscribe
- `GET /ports/` — Port list
- `GET /ports/congestion/` — Ports ranked by congestion score
- `GET /ports/analytics/` — Aggregated analytics for dashboards
- `GET /voyages/` — All voyages
- `GET /voyages/<id>/replay/` — Voyage replay waypoints
- `GET /safety-events/` — Active safety zones
- [simulate_live_api.py](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/vessels/management/commands/simulate_live_api.py) — Continuous AIS position simulator (background command)

### Milestone 4 — Frontend Integration & UI Polish
- **Home Page** — Hero section with animated radar, statistics, call to action
- **Live Map** — Leaflet map with custom SVG vessel markers, safety event circles, auto-refresh
- **Vessels Page** — Searchable/filterable table with subscribe/unsubscribe per row
- **Vessel Detail Page** — Full vessel info, recent events, OpenStreetMap link
- **Ports Page** — Congestion dashboard with color-coded status bars, sorted table
- **Analytics Dashboard** — Bar chart (top congested ports), Pie charts (vessel types, voyage statuses)
- **Voyage Replay** — Timeline stepper with play/pause, per-waypoint event details
- **Dashboard** — User overview, notifications, subscribed vessels
- **Admin Tools Panel** — API status cards, safety event table, quick links

### Bug Fixes Applied
- Fixed `vessel_type` → `type` field name bug in [PortAnalyticsView](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/backend/apps/ports/views.py#71-128) (analytics charts were showing zero/empty data)
- Fixed all emojis across the entire frontend (replaced with SVG icons and styled dots)
- Fixed `venv_win/` being tracked by git (added to [.gitignore](file:///c:/Users/LENOVO/Desktop/teamm3/Maritime-Vessel-Tracking/.gitignore), prevented future corruption)
- Fixed PortsPage error state — now shows a "Retry" button instead of a dead screen
- Backend startup fixed to use system Python when `venv_win` is unavailable

