## 8. How to Run

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.11+
- Node.js 18+
- All Python packages installed globally or in a venv: `django`, `djangorestframework`, `djangorestframework-simplejwt`, `django-cors-headers`, `python-dotenv`

### Step 1 — Database Setup (first time only)
```powershell
cd C:\Users\LENOVO\Desktop\teamm3\Maritime-Vessel-Tracking\backend
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py seed_large_data --clear
```

### Step 2 — Start Backend Server
```powershell
cd C:\Users\LENOVO\Desktop\teamm3\Maritime-Vessel-Tracking\backend
python manage.py runserver 8000
# Backend: http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

### Step 3 — Start Frontend
```powershell
cd C:\Users\LENOVO\Desktop\teamm3\Maritime-Vessel-Tracking\frontend
npm install   # first time only
npm run dev
# Frontend: http://localhost:5173
```

### Step 4 — Start Live Data Simulator (optional)
```powershell
cd C:\Users\LENOVO\Desktop\teamm3\Maritime-Vessel-Tracking\backend
python manage.py simulate_live_api --interval 8 --batch 10
```

### Quick Links When Running
| Service | URL |
|---|---|
| Frontend App | http://localhost:5173 |
| Backend API | http://127.0.0.1:8000 |
| Django Admin | http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/ |
| Vessels API | http://127.0.0.1:8000/vessels/ |
| Ports Congestion | http://127.0.0.1:8000/ports/congestion/ |
| Analytics | http://127.0.0.1:8000/ports/analytics/ |
| Safety Events | http://127.0.0.1:8000/safety-events/ |
| Voyages | http://127.0.0.1:8000/voyages/ |

